Chapter: NetPollClamped
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Net chapter NetDriver

 The poll cell is 32 bits of memory and `net-driver-poll-interval` is a
 `peek-32` of it, so this pokes the cell directly rather than arranging a
 calibration: the subject is what the READER does with a value, not how the
 value got there.

 Three arms, and the middle one is why the other two mean anything. A reader
 that answered the fallback unconditionally would pass both clamp arms and
 fail `in-range`; a reader with no clamps at all passes `in-range` and fails
 both others.

 `above` is the arm the ceiling was added for: 3,000,000,000 fits in the cell
 and cannot come from calibration, which adds `net-driver-cal-batch` at most
 `net-driver-cal-fuel` times.

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let lo = poke-32 net-driver-poll-cell 0 10
    in print-line-uni ("below   : " & show net-driver-poll-interval)
    let mid = poke-32 net-driver-poll-cell 0 1758000
    in print-line-uni ("in-range: " & show net-driver-poll-interval)
    let hi = poke-32 net-driver-poll-cell 0 3000000000
    in print-line-uni ("above   : " & show net-driver-poll-interval)
    print-line-uni ("cal-max : " & show net-driver-cal-max)
  end

